WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.242 --> 00:00:02.340
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:04.290
- Not all lawyers are good.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.510
I cannot emphasize this enough,

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:09.300
and not all lawsuits are well stated.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.190
That is doubly true.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:14.820
And while you have a constitutional
right to a jury trial,

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.590
I have a first amendment right

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:18.000
to make fun of you mercilessly

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.024
in front of millions of subscribers.

00:00:21.024 --> 00:00:23.520
(man laughs)

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:24.353
Now in fairness,

00:00:24.353 --> 00:00:25.890
frivolous lawsuits are often brought

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:27.690
by self-represented individuals

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:28.980
who are unable to find a lawyer

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:30.360
to take their crazy cases.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.670
But sometimes there are actual attorneys

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.410
who are willing to attach their names

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:36.060
and reputations to the lawsuits

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:38.370
that we're going to destroy today.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.800
So let's start with the
case of the candy box

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.900
that has too much air in it.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.180
A time honored tradition
of going to the movies,

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:46.590
is buying movie candy

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:49.020
and one of the more popular movie candies

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.890
for inexplicable reasons, is Junior Mints,

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:54.070
the candy that tastes

00:00:54.919 --> 00:00:56.010
like you just went to the dentist office.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:58.620
Now, if you've ever picked
up a box of Junior Mints,

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:01.350
you might have noticed that
the box is not exactly filled

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:03.240
to the top with candy.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:05.010
For many, this is an irritating example

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:06.000
of shrinkflation

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.700
where companies downsize
the size or quantity

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:09.870
of the product that you receive

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:11.700
while charging the same amount of money.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.830
And if you've ever gone
to a movie theater,

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:15.630
you're being charged way, way too much

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:17.490
for basically mint flavored wax.

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:19.680
But for New York City
resident Biola Daniel,

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.040
the air in the Junior Mint's
package was an egregious fraud

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.900
perpetrated upon the American public.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.100
And for that injustice,

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.710
Ms. Daniel and her lawyers
decided to take a stand

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:30.450
for consumers everywhere.

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:33.180
So in 2017, Ms. Daniel
filed a class action lawsuit

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:34.350
against Tutsi Role Industries,

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:36.480
the parent company of Junior Mints,

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:39.360
claiming the manufacturer
intentionally tricks customers

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:42.570
by packaging their candies
in unexpectedly large boxes

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:44.280
topped with too much air,

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:46.440
referred to in the
complaint as slack fill.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:47.790
- [Man] So as I move this up and down,

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:49.830
it's gonna pump air out of the jar.

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:51.060
- Abel Durin of New York

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.680
and Tequila Perkins of Mississippi

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:55.020
but later join the lawsuit
as class plaintiffs.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:56.730
According to the 36 page complaint,

00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:59.640
Ms. Daniel purchased a 3.5
ounce box of Junior Mints

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:02.820
from a local pharmacy for $1.49.

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:04.387
Ms. Daniel complained that the box

00:02:04.387 --> 00:02:07.980
"Contained approximately
40% nonfunctional slack fill

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:10.860
while competitor candies like
Milk Duds and Good and Plenty

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:14.220
only contained 23 and 12%
slack fill respectively.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.050
In addition to those candies

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:19.140
actually being something
a human should consume.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:21.570
The complaint said, "The
science of the products boxes

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:24.158
in comparison to the volume of
the candy contained therein,

00:02:24.158 --> 00:02:26.550
makes it appear to
plaintiff and class members

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:29.340
that they are buying more than
what is actually being sold.

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:31.860
Plaintiff and class members
are denied the benefit

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:32.693
of their bargain

00:02:32.693 --> 00:02:35.160
because they pay for a
full box of the product

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:37.290
but actually received far less."

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.870
But US District Judge
Naomi Reese Buchwald,

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:42.390
disagreed tossing the
complaint 10 months later.

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:45.690
In her 44 page ruling dripping with shade,

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:46.710
Judge Buchwald determined

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:48.990
that there was no fraud
in Junior Mints packaging

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:50.610
and ripped the plaintiffs for claiming

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:53.640
that they had been intentionally
deceived by slack fill.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.500
The judge argued that
there was no deception

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:58.080
because reasonable consumers
of ordinary intelligence,

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.970
could have determined
the amount of the candies

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:01.567
from reading the box.

00:03:01.567 --> 00:03:03.330
"The law simply does not provide the level

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:05.280
of coddling the plaintiffs seek,

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.080
assuming that a reasonable consumer

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.820
might ignore the evidence
plainly before him,

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:11.130
attributes to consumers
a level of stupidity

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:13.380
that the court cannot countenance."

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:14.490
And according to Reuters,

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:16.110
hundreds of slack fill lawsuits

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:17.490
have been filed in recent years.

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:18.750
And in the last decade alone,

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:21.540
Tutsi Roll LLC has faced
five separate lawsuits

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:24.510
over air in its candy boxes
with judges in California

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:26.040
New York, Illinois, and New Jersey,

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:27.600
all dismissing these cases.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:29.400
Now, to be fair to the
class plaintiffs here,

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.590
it's not impossible to win these lawsuits.

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:32.520
According to the FDA,

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.380
a container that does
not allow the consumer

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.060
to fully view its contents,

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:39.030
shall be considered to be
filled as to be misleading

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.340
if it contains nonfunctional slack fill.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:42.270
Slack fill is the difference

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:44.160
between the actual
capacity of the container

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.560
and the volume of product
contained they're in.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.210
And the slack fill is nonfunctional

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:49.830
if it is filled to less the capacity

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:51.300
for reasons other than one,

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.340
the protection of the
contents of the package.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:55.320
Two, the requirements of the machines used

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:57.480
for enclosing the
contents in such package.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:59.430
Three, unavoidable product settling

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:00.840
during shipping and handling.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.370
Four, the need for the package

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:03.750
to perform a specific function.

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:05.220
Five, the fact that the product consists

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.800
of a food packaged in a reusable container

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:10.011
or six, the inability to
increase level of fill

00:04:10.011 --> 00:04:13.140
or to further reduce
the size of the package.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:14.430
But under these circumstances,

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:16.260
it looks like these judges have determined

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:21.260
that slack-fill lawsuits
are full of hot air, get it?

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:22.787
Am I right?

00:04:22.787 --> 00:04:23.790
(people booing)

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:26.670
Okay, fine, boo me for my amazing puns.

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:29.130
I can hear you through the computer.

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:31.290
But that takes us to
the Minnesota magician

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:33.630
who sued David Copperfield and David Blain

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:35.790
for stealing his godly powers.

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:40.456
- [Man 2] Hell yeah, I
have the power of God.

00:04:40.456 --> 00:04:41.744
(tractor engine roars)

00:04:41.744 --> 00:04:42.660
- Now, you've probably heard

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:44.100
that he off repeated Axiom,

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:47.280
that people who choose to
represent themselves in court,

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:49.770
well, they have a fool for a client.

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:51.540
But enter Christopher Roller,

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:53.610
a Minnesota magician who decided

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:55.530
that he would also be that fool

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:59.490
by repeatedly suing famous
magician David Copperfield

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:01.020
for millions of dollars.

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:03.240
On what grounds you may ask?

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:06.390
Well, for stealing Roller's
godlike magician powers

00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:08.640
without just compensation?

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:11.550
Obviously, now the saga
began in March of 2005

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:13.440
when Roller sued David Copperfield

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:15.367
in Minnesota Federal court.

00:05:15.367 --> 00:05:18.360
"David Copperfield has
been using my godly powers

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:19.800
to perform his magic."

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:22.140
The complaint begins
before directing the court

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:23.999
to his website, so it may witness Rollers,

00:05:23.999 --> 00:05:26.670
"Journey to godliness."

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:28.740
Citing UFO videos as proof

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:31.050
that godly powers exist on earth.

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:34.147
Roller argues that magicians
including Copperfield,

00:05:34.147 --> 00:05:38.310
"Have also been granted
Godly powers by me somehow,

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:40.380
but they have been keeping it as secret

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:42.687
and keeping the credits from me."

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:47.940
Roller who claims he's been
secretly filmed for decades,

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:49.140
all of the "Truman Show."

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:51.270
- Good afternoon, good
evening, and good night.

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:53.730
- Is an avid conspiracy theorist

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:55.560
if you didn't guess that already

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:58.830
with a history of filing
bizarre frivolous lawsuits

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:02.130
like in 2007 when he sued
then President George W. Bush

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:03.720
and Vice President Dick Chaney,

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:07.800
for conspiring with, "Fellow
demons to have roller murdered

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.930
with an explosive vice at a red lobster."

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:10.950
In Roller's complaint,

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:14.430
he graciously gives Copperfield
a way out of the litigation

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:16.500
to reveal his magician secrets

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:19.770
that prove Copperfield's tricks/illusions

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:23.400
are done conventionally
and without godly powers.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.807
But Roller lamented that he has,

00:06:25.807 --> 00:06:27.750
"Politely asked David via email

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:31.050
to show how his tricks are
done with no response."

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:33.481
I guess Mr. Copperfield
just doesn't have time

00:06:33.481 --> 00:06:35.250
for Roller's tricks.

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:37.470
- I Don't have time for your magic tricks.

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:40.590
- Illusions dad, you don't
have time for my illusion.

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:42.180
- Now, Roller who has never worked

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:44.160
for Copperfield in any capacity,

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:47.220
claimed the magician had
violated Minnesota labor law

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:48.360
by stealing his magic,

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:52.740
thus entirely roller to
a modest $50 million,

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:56.490
10% of all past/future career earnings.

00:06:56.490 --> 00:06:58.680
And in 2006, the Minnesota Court

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:00.390
summarily dismissed Roller's case

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:02.190
for failure to state a claim.

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:03.150
But believe it or not,

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:07.650
Roller saga against David
Copperfield actually gets weirder.

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:08.820
In June of 2005,

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:11.190
Roller attempted to
patent his magic powers.

00:07:11.190 --> 00:07:12.300
In his patent application,

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:14.047
Roller refers to himself as a,

00:07:14.047 --> 00:07:16.470
"godly entity who seeks
the exclusive right

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:18.510
to the ethical use and financial gain

00:07:18.510 --> 00:07:21.660
in the use of godly
powers on planet Earth."

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:24.870
Roller then sued David
Copperfield again in federal court

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:26.430
this time for patent infringement.

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:28.980
And while motion to dismiss
the case was pending,

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:30.630
Roller filed an amended complaint,

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:31.740
alleging that Copperfield

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:33.330
and at least three other defendants

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:36.180
were engaged in a
conspiracy to murder him."

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:38.370
So in November, 2007,

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:40.920
the federal court again
dismissed Roller's claim

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:43.380
with prejudice and barred
the fictious litigant

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:45.450
from ever suing Copperfield again.

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:47.400
And here's a pro tip,

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.320
even if you had godly powers

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:50.610
that would not entitle you

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:52.274
to a patent on those godly powers,

00:07:52.274 --> 00:07:57.210
which by the way would
expire after 17 years.

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:59.550
So I'm getting that this guy

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:01.890
has not put everything together,

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:04.140
but the court dismissed the
patent infringement claim

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:05.700
on the grounds that the patent actually

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:06.690
had not been granted

00:08:06.690 --> 00:08:09.120
and thus roller had no patent rights

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:10.740
that could be infringed.

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:13.140
The court also found that
there were zero facts

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:14.490
to support the claim that Copperfield

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:17.160
was involved in a murderous
conspiracy against Roller.

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:20.880
And to add insult to injury in 2008,

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:22.380
the US patent and trademark office,

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:24.217
rejected Roller's patent writing,

00:08:24.217 --> 00:08:26.310
"The specification has not described

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:27.990
how one of ordinary skill

00:08:27.990 --> 00:08:32.070
and the art could make or use
the claimed godly powers."

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:35.340
And in a near identical
lawsuit filed in June, 2005,

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:38.430
Roller sued magician David
Blain for $2 million,

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:41.160
accusing the magician of
stealing Roller's godly powers

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:42.420
to perform his magic.

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:44.460
- Are you sure you
didn't buy a teddy bear?

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.050
- Yes, I'm sure I didn't.

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:46.938
- Teddy bear.

00:08:46.938 --> 00:08:48.252
- [All] What the f?

00:08:48.252 --> 00:08:49.085
- How did you.

00:08:49.085 --> 00:08:50.310
- But the court dismissed that lawsuit

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:51.660
as well due to Roller's failure

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:53.730
to serve Mr. Blaine with the complaint.

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:57.300
And that's the thing about
trying to sue a magician,

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:59.520
they'll just disappear on you.

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:02.280
But that takes us to the
lawsuit of the Oregon man

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:03.690
who filed a billion dollar lawsuit

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:06.990
because Michael Jordan sorta
kind of maybe looks like him.

00:09:06.990 --> 00:09:08.160
Now, as you probably know,

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:10.920
few people have embodied the greatness

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:12.930
of sports like basketball superstar

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:15.390
and popular meme template, Michael Jordan.

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:17.370
As the iconic basketball player

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:20.340
who earned six championship
rings with the Chicago Bulls

00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:21.720
and nab to starting role

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:24.210
in the critically unclaimed "Space Jam."

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:28.830
Many have credited MJ as
the true goat of the NBA.

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:29.663
- It's just funny

00:09:29.663 --> 00:09:32.060
'cause I don't remember
Jordan winning championships

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:34.160
with two different teams.

00:09:37.007 --> 00:09:38.160
- Oh (beep).

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:40.620
- But contrary to the iconic
90s Gatorade commercial,

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:42.990
not everyone wanted to be like Mike,

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:45.900
especially not Portland,
Oregon resident, Alan Heckard,

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:48.750
who claimed that his life
had been completely ruined

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:51.000
after being mistaken for
the basketball champion

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:52.980
nearly every day for 15 years.

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:55.410
And argued to an actual court of law

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:58.571
that Michael Jordan and Nike
owed him nearly $1 billion

00:09:58.571 --> 00:10:03.570
for his horrific
injustice because America.

00:10:03.570 --> 00:10:07.830
In 2006, Heckard sued Michael
Jordan for 416 million,

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:09.630
arguing that the "Space Jam" star

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:12.600
was liable to Heckard for
emotional pain and suffering,

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:14.760
defamation and permanent injury.

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:16.920
Heckard acting as his own attorney,

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:19.170
I probably don't need to tell you,

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:20.947
alleged the following in the complaint;

00:10:20.947 --> 00:10:23.430
"Whatever public functions he attends,

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:27.420
people are continually on
a daily basis harassing him

00:10:27.420 --> 00:10:29.190
of looking like Michael Jordan.

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:31.620
These unpleasant feelings from the public

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:33.030
have trouble Heckard's nerves

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:36.217
and denied him the right
to a piece of mind."

00:10:36.217 --> 00:10:40.290
#youhavenolegalright
to that piece of mind.

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:42.570
Now, Heckard also sued
Nike founder Phil Knight

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:44.700
for 416 million as well,

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:46.297
writing in the complaint that Knight,

00:10:46.297 --> 00:10:49.920
"Contributed to turning
Michael Jordan into a legend

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:53.250
which forced Heckard to
change his appearance."

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.470
In interviews, Heckard
asserted the resemblance

00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:57.090
to Michael Jordan was so powerful

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:58.890
that he would frequently draw crowds

00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:01.800
of disappointed Jordan fans
whenever he went to church

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:04.297
or played basketball in the park.

00:11:04.297 --> 00:11:06.120
"It's making life uncomfortable.

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:07.890
I'm constantly being harassed.

00:11:07.890 --> 00:11:09.900
I should be able to enjoy my own life

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:11.100
but everywhere I go,

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:13.860
people tell me I look exactly like him."

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:16.860
Now, Heckard arguably
bears some resemblance

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:20.220
to MJ with a shaved head
and earring on his left ear

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:23.580
and similar conditioning from
playing amateur basketball.

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:26.393
But it should also be noted

00:11:26.393 --> 00:11:29.280
that the 51 year old shuttle bus driver,

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:31.920
is eight years older than Michael Jordan.

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:35.640
And at six feet tall stands
a full six inches shorter

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:38.010
than the six time NBA champion.

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:39.270
And in this lawyer's opinion,

00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:41.820
the gentleman from Portland
should be flattered

00:11:41.820 --> 00:11:46.110
that anyone should mistake him
for Michael freaking Jordan

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:47.790
on the basketball court.

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:49.410
But Heckard did not find

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:51.480
the comparison complimentary at all.

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:53.190
Now, when asked how he arrived

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:55.500
at the damages amount of 416 million,

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:56.505
Heckard told the media,

00:11:56.505 --> 00:11:58.440
"Well, you figure with my age

00:11:58.440 --> 00:12:00.330
and you multiply that times seven

00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:02.670
and then I turn around

00:12:02.670 --> 00:12:07.530
and I figure that's what
it all boils down to."

00:12:07.530 --> 00:12:12.330
Yeah, so that's not how
calculating damages works

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:14.760
or for that matter math.

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:16.320
But you don't need a
law degree to understand

00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:17.490
why no lawyer agreed

00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:20.250
to take such a patently
frivolous defamation case.

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:21.480
to assert a claim for defamation,

00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:23.040
a plaintiff has to show that the defendant

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:24.570
made a false statement of fact

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:26.280
about the plaintiff to a third party

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:28.890
and this false statement
caused harm to the plaintiff.

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:30.540
Now, I probably don't need to tell you

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:32.880
that being repeatedly
confused for celebrity,

00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:35.580
does not come close to being defamatory,

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:38.940
especially when there's no
evidence anyone did anything

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:41.411
to propagate the falsehood.

00:12:41.411 --> 00:12:42.420
And it's not even a falsehood.

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:44.580
It's like when people say
that I look like Ryan Reynolds

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:45.960
or John Krasinski.

00:12:45.960 --> 00:12:49.620
That's whatever the
opposite of defamation is.

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:50.497
Now when people say,

00:12:50.497 --> 00:12:52.890
"I look like a Disney character

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:55.350
or a dad from a Pixar movie"

00:12:55.350 --> 00:12:56.940
that is defamation.

00:12:56.940 --> 00:12:59.940
- I don't know where this
disrespectful attitude came from.

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:02.550
- But Heckard doesn't
allege that Michael Jordan

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:05.370
or Nike falsely claimed that
Heckard is Michael Jordan.

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:07.830
So this is not defamation.

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:10.350
The complaint, much like
Heckard's damages calculation,

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:13.530
is essentially just the
underpants knowns of lawsuit.

00:13:13.530 --> 00:13:15.300
- Phase one, collect underpants,

00:13:15.300 --> 00:13:19.350
phase two, phase three, profit.

00:13:19.350 --> 00:13:20.183
- I get it.

00:13:20.183 --> 00:13:22.410
- Now, weeks later, Heckard
would spared the legal system

00:13:22.410 --> 00:13:24.518
and further drama by
withdrawing the lawsuit

00:13:24.518 --> 00:13:26.190
without explanation.

00:13:26.190 --> 00:13:29.310
But the explanation is, it
was a frivolous lawsuit.

00:13:29.310 --> 00:13:30.870
But that takes us to the firefighter

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:35.370
who was afraid to enter burning
buildings for fear of fire.

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:36.630
Now, when pollsters ask people

00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:39.180
to name the most trusted
and admired professions,

00:13:39.180 --> 00:13:41.880
you'll often find firefighters
at the top of the list.

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:43.890
Perhaps it's because they're like police

00:13:43.890 --> 00:13:47.110
but they don't have a gun
with which to kill you.

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:50.190
But who doesn't love firefighters.

00:13:50.190 --> 00:13:51.900
When they aren't saving cats from trees

00:13:51.900 --> 00:13:53.760
or posing for hunky calendars,

00:13:53.760 --> 00:13:56.910
firefighters are famous for
charging into burning buildings

00:13:56.910 --> 00:13:59.190
to rescue those in harm's way.

00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:01.042
But one Texas firefighter,

00:14:01.042 --> 00:14:03.240
trying to claim that his fear

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:04.830
of charging into burning buildings,

00:14:04.830 --> 00:14:06.540
was equivalent to illegal disability

00:14:06.540 --> 00:14:08.580
and his removal from the front lines

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:11.580
was illegal disability discrimination.

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:13.440
A spoiler, he lost.

00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:14.790
Enter Shayn Proler,

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:16.710
a Captain of the Houston Fire Department,

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:18.600
leader of a fire suppression crew

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:21.180
who had one teeny tiny problem.

00:14:21.180 --> 00:14:22.860
He was afraid of fire,

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:23.693
for example, in 2004,

00:14:23.693 --> 00:14:25.440
Proler arrived at the scene of a fire

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:26.820
and was unable to enter the building.

00:14:26.820 --> 00:14:28.620
In 2006 during a house fire,

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:30.120
Proler was so frightened
that he was unable

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:32.280
to put on his firefighting
gear, take orders,

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:33.630
or even walk properly.

00:14:33.630 --> 00:14:34.770
A doctor determined Proler

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:36.510
experienced a temporary memory loss

00:14:36.510 --> 00:14:38.760
called global transient amnesia.

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:40.290
The city then Reassigned Proler

00:14:40.290 --> 00:14:42.480
to Firefighting Training Academy.

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:43.830
Proler responded by filing

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:45.570
a successful administrative appeal,

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:48.360
after which he was returned
to the fire suppression crew.

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:50.250
And when the city took it to trial,

00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:51.690
Proler filed a counterclaim,

00:14:51.690 --> 00:14:54.000
arguing that his
reassignment violated laws

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:56.010
against disability discrimination.

00:14:56.010 --> 00:14:57.900
Proler did not claim he was disabled,

00:14:57.900 --> 00:15:01.170
just that the city of Houston
perceived him to be disabled,

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:03.180
making his reassignment a violation

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:05.460
of state and federal
anti-discrimination laws.

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:09.720
The jury agreed awarding
Proler $362,000 in damages.

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:11.190
The case was appealed all the way

00:15:11.190 --> 00:15:12.420
to the Texas Supreme Court,

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:14.100
which throughout the jury verdict.

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:15.360
In the supreme court's opinion,

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:17.130
the court highlighted
that anti disability laws

00:15:17.130 --> 00:15:19.200
do not protect every
person who wants a job,

00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:20.550
but who lacks the mental, physical,

00:15:20.550 --> 00:15:23.610
or experiential skill to
perform that particular job.

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:25.200
To illustrate the point that court argued

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:28.350
that lacking the skills to
play for the San Antonio Spurs,

00:15:28.350 --> 00:15:30.690
does not mean a person is disabled.

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:31.830
Accordingly, the court concluded

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:34.200
that there was not a scintilla of evidence

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:38.130
that the fearful fire
captain was disabled.

00:15:38.130 --> 00:15:40.920
Proler then argued that
even if he was not disabled,

00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:42.267
the city perceived him as such

00:15:42.267 --> 00:15:45.930
and thus is liable for taking
an adverse employment action,

00:15:45.930 --> 00:15:49.320
namely by reassigning him based
on the perceived disability.

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:50.490
The court rejected this argument

00:15:50.490 --> 00:15:53.130
that there was no basis for
classifying Proler's fear

00:15:53.130 --> 00:15:55.042
as a disability.

00:15:55.042 --> 00:15:57.450
Disability was defined as being regarded

00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:59.430
as having a mental or physical impairment

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:02.340
that substantially limits at
least one major life activity.

00:16:02.340 --> 00:16:05.193
And major life activity
refers to basic functions

00:16:05.193 --> 00:16:09.240
like taking care of yourself,
walking, seeing, thinking,

00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:10.350
and breathing.

00:16:10.350 --> 00:16:11.400
Now under these definitions,

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:13.800
the court held that there was
no disability discrimination

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:14.850
against the fearful firemen

00:16:14.850 --> 00:16:18.150
because, "Fighting fires is
not a major life activity."

00:16:18.150 --> 00:16:19.950
The court also found that Proler's fear

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:21.300
of entering burning buildings

00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:24.325
was not a disability to be
discriminated against noting,

00:16:24.325 --> 00:16:27.330
"A reluctance to charge
into a burning building,

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:29.220
is not a mental impairment at all,

00:16:29.220 --> 00:16:31.170
it's the normal human response.

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:34.590
Such a reluctance cannot be
characterized as an impairment,

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:35.850
much less an impairment

00:16:35.850 --> 00:16:38.460
that substantially limits
a major life activity."

00:16:38.460 --> 00:16:40.140
But if you're bitter over that lawsuit,

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:42.150
that's nothing compared to the bitterness

00:16:42.150 --> 00:16:44.430
that a certain Austin resident felt

00:16:44.430 --> 00:16:46.650
for a date who texted during a movie

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:50.790
and for whom he sued for $17.31.

00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:52.260
Now, when it comes to finding love,

00:16:52.260 --> 00:16:55.110
there's nothing more
exhilarating and nerve wracking

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:56.460
than the first date.

00:16:56.460 --> 00:16:59.130
The excitement and promise
of a lasting connection,

00:16:59.130 --> 00:17:00.210
tempered by the dread

00:17:00.210 --> 00:17:02.790
that this will end in
disappointment like all others

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:07.410
or end in a lawsuit
against you for texting.

00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:08.580
But that's exactly what happened

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:10.770
when Brandon Vezmer turned
to dispute over a date,

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:11.910
texting during a movie

00:17:11.910 --> 00:17:15.990
into a legal dispute by
suing her for $17.31,

00:17:15.990 --> 00:17:17.400
the cost of the movie.

00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:20.666
Here's what happened, in May
of 2017, 37 year old Vezmer

00:17:20.666 --> 00:17:22.080
took a 35 year old woman

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:25.470
who I'm just gonna call Nola Exit

00:17:25.470 --> 00:17:27.510
to see "Guardian to the Galaxy Volume two"

00:17:27.510 --> 00:17:28.860
in 3D in Austin, Texas.

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:32.880
Everything was going fine
until Miss Exit began to text.

00:17:32.880 --> 00:17:34.927
The way that Vezmer put it,

00:17:34.927 --> 00:17:37.140
"It was kind of a first date from hell.

00:17:37.140 --> 00:17:40.120
This is like one of my
biggest pet peeves."

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:43.260
Yes, I'm sure that it
was just horrible for him

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:46.470
and this poor woman was
having the time of her life

00:17:46.470 --> 00:17:48.900
and was being completely inconsiderate.

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:51.990
Now, after suggesting that
Ms. Exit step outside to text,

00:17:51.990 --> 00:17:53.703
when she refused to stop,

00:17:54.570 --> 00:17:55.740
she then left the theater

00:17:55.740 --> 00:17:59.490
and never came back leaving
Vezmer to find his own ride

00:17:59.490 --> 00:18:00.690
'cause yeah, that checks out.

00:18:00.690 --> 00:18:02.160
Now, according to text messages posted

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:03.900
on his now defunct Twitter account,

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:07.080
Vezmer demanded that she
pay $17 for the movie ticket

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:10.020
and $4 for the slice of
pizza that he bought her

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:12.840
or else he would take her
to small claims court.

00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:15.420
Ms. Exit likely assumed that
this was an empty threat.

00:18:15.420 --> 00:18:19.170
I mean, who would haul someone
into small claims court

00:18:19.170 --> 00:18:21.870
over a bogus $20 claim?

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:24.060
But apparently that person was none other

00:18:24.060 --> 00:18:25.410
than her date Vezmer.

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:26.820
In his petition Vezmer alleged

00:18:26.820 --> 00:18:29.010
that Ms. Exit used her phone to read

00:18:29.010 --> 00:18:30.120
and send text messages

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:33.720
at least 10 to 20 times in 15 minutes.

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:36.030
In direct violation of
the theater's policy,

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:37.890
adversely affecting the viewing experience

00:18:37.890 --> 00:18:39.930
of plaintiff and others.

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:43.260
Vezmer asked the court
for $17.31 in compensation

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:44.430
for defendant movie ticket,

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:48.180
dropping his initial $4
demand for the pizza.

00:18:48.180 --> 00:18:51.157
He closed his petition in
dramatic fashion writing,

00:18:51.157 --> 00:18:52.950
"While damages sought are modest

00:18:52.950 --> 00:18:54.360
to the principle is important

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:58.920
as defendant's behavior is a
threat to civilized society."

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:03.317
So you can save civilized
society for $17.31?

00:19:05.130 --> 00:19:07.170
That's kind of a bargain
when you put it that way.

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:08.640
Now the story immediately went viral

00:19:08.640 --> 00:19:10.440
with The AV Club calling him a hero

00:19:10.440 --> 00:19:12.090
and "Guardian's" Director, James Gunn,

00:19:12.090 --> 00:19:15.030
cheekly suggesting that Vezmer's
date deserved jail time.

00:19:15.030 --> 00:19:17.550
But not everyone was
cheering, "Let's go Brandon,"

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:20.520
especially the poor woman
who went on this date.

00:19:20.520 --> 00:19:23.160
When the Austin American
statesman informed her

00:19:23.160 --> 00:19:26.490
about the lawsuit, she replied,
"Oh my God, this is crazy."

00:19:26.490 --> 00:19:28.470
She then disputed Vezmer's claim

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:29.850
that she texted 10 to 15 times,

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:32.299
saying she only sent two texts to a friend

00:19:32.299 --> 00:19:34.050
in a fight with her boyfriend

00:19:34.050 --> 00:19:36.960
and kept her phone low to
ensure no one was disturbed.

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:39.268
She then issued a statement
to a local news station,

00:19:39.268 --> 00:19:41.730
"I did have a very brief date with Brandon

00:19:41.730 --> 00:19:43.560
that I chose to end prematurely.

00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:46.110
His behavior made me
extremely uncomfortable

00:19:46.110 --> 00:19:48.090
and I felt I needed to remove myself

00:19:48.090 --> 00:19:50.070
from the situation for my own safety.

00:19:50.070 --> 00:19:52.410
He has escalated situation far past

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:54.600
what any mentally healthy person would.

00:19:54.600 --> 00:19:57.210
I feel sorry that I hurt
his feelings badly enough

00:19:57.210 --> 00:19:59.340
that he felt he needed
to commit so much time

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:01.020
and effort into seeking revenge.

00:20:01.020 --> 00:20:02.850
I hope one day he can move past this

00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:04.740
and find peace in his life."

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:05.940
Yeah, why am I not surprised

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:09.060
that this guy completely
misread the situation?

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:10.980
I guess it might have been a tip off

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:12.540
that he filed a lawsuit

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:16.170
that had no legal merit
whatsoever purely out of spite.

00:20:16.170 --> 00:20:17.010
I guess that, yeah,

00:20:17.010 --> 00:20:18.660
that probably should have
tipped me off to that.

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:21.630
Now this matter was
finally settled in a sense,

00:20:21.630 --> 00:20:23.070
thanks to Inside Edition

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:23.970
who arranged for the pair

00:20:23.970 --> 00:20:25.890
to meet outside the original movie theater

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:28.830
because that worked the first time.

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:32.407
She ended up paying this
guy $17.31 telling him,

00:20:32.407 --> 00:20:34.140
"The date just didn't work out.

00:20:34.140 --> 00:20:35.310
Just leave this alone."

00:20:35.310 --> 00:20:37.470
And while Vezmer did drop the suit,

00:20:37.470 --> 00:20:39.240
he stands by his conduct.

00:20:39.240 --> 00:20:41.743
- Count it right, just to
make sure it's all here.

00:20:41.743 --> 00:20:45.270
10, 15, 16, 17, 31 cents.

00:20:45.270 --> 00:20:46.980
- And Vezmer issued a statement

00:20:46.980 --> 00:20:48.607
that he wanted people to,

00:20:48.607 --> 00:20:51.540
"Treat other people with
respect and dignity."

00:20:51.540 --> 00:20:53.400
Exactly the kind of respect and dignity

00:20:53.400 --> 00:20:56.790
that is not commensurate with
filing a bull (beep) lawsuit

00:20:56.790 --> 00:20:59.040
out of revenge, sorry Brandon.

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:00.004
- It's settled.

